- The historical evidence from Pavel Stroev's *Spiski ierarkhov i nastoyateley monastyrey rossiyskoy tserkvi* conclusively identifies Veniamin (Sakhnovsky) as the archimandrite of the Pskov-Caves Monastery from 1730 until his consecration as Bishop of Kolomna on July 25, 1731.
- The alternative claims regarding Markell Radyshevsky conflate his external political disputes and separate monastic posts with Pskov-Caves, where he does not appear in official abbatial succession records.
- The correct choice remains G (Veniamin).
}
